    description: "TypeScript interface method overloads do not hash their type-parameter clause, so bound-only interface overloads would tie.\n\nWI-bubak (PR 3 commit 315063612) wired the positional type-parameter-clause hash for Java, Groovy, Kotlin, Scala, Swift and C#, not TypeScript. Measured 0 bound-only tie groups on koel (528 files, 4,306 callables) and nest/packages (819 files, 7,545 callables), so it was not wired. Interface method overloads are the only TS overloads emitted as separate symbols. Kept open as a stated limit; counter at /home/jgstern_agent/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/agent5/count_bound_ties_ts.py."  # a7e8
